Read-me file for momond 0.6

  This is my first contribution to the linux world. It isnt too much, and
  probably it is plenty of coding mistakes.
  momond ( modem monitor daemon ) , ir is based in  momon-2.01  , written by 
  Klaus Luft ( Klaus.Luft@stud.uni-karlsruhe.de ).

  momond uses the classes defined by Klaus Luft to check the status of the 
  modem line and calculates the cost of all outgoing calls, based on the 
  new telephone rates of German Telekom from the first January 1996.  I am 
  looking for people who want to add support for telephon rates of other 
  countries.

  momond is distributed under the terms of the GPL (GNU Public License ). 
  It is only 14Kb big, and seems to work well under Linux. It uses ioctl to
  get the status of the modem.

  Try it, and send me your comments. momon-0.6 is still in beta status, so 
  i need people that want to improve it or to suggest new features.

  You can find it in :

    ftp.fh-wuerzburg.de/incoming/momond-*.tar.gz

    ( I am still looking for a better place )


COMMANDS
- --------
   momond is able to read commands passed to a fifo special file ( named
   pipe ) . The commands are read by momond in a transparent way, from 
   this file. To send a command to momond you have to write to that file 
   the command you want momond to execute:

   echo command > <fifo_special_file>

   Where command is one of:

   01234       This is, a number from 0 to 4 , to change the zone tarif
               rate.
   T           Start the on-line counter. This is useful to use momond
               with voice call. In this version is included an small script
               which shows how it works.
   H           Finish to count the time on-line for voice calls.
   Rxxxxx      Dial the tfn number xxxx . It is used for voice calls.
  
INSTALLATION
- ------------

  1. Edit the file main.cpp and change the default modem device, and log file
  2. Compile it with 'make'
  3. Be sure that the user who runs momond is able to read the modem device
     ( it wont work 'setuid' !! )
  4. Be sure that the log file exists and is writable 
  5. Start momond
  6. Write something in the pipe 

PROBLEMS ( or features ? :) )
- --------

   Momond wont start to work until it has something to read in the 
   named pipe. So , you have to send first a command to the pipe ( why
   not the tarif base ? ) to make it work. 

TO DO
- -----

*  Improve quantity and quality of the log messages
*  Allow it to communicate with other programs that want to show the status of
   the modem line ( Spent money, last call , time on line , ... ) 
*  Write a man page ( i don't know how to make it )
*  Write documentation as well in German
*  Add support for external telephone rates file 


That's all folks !

Enrique Melero
