I'm announcing the beta release of EZWGL, the EZ widget and
graphics library written under Xlib (R5/6).

EZWGL implements a few Motif like widgets and a few OpenGL like
graphics commands. It runs on displays with  >= 8 bit deep
visuals. It has been tested on Sun Sparc, Sgi Indigo, Dec Alpha
and Pentium Linux.

Currently implemented widgets are:

   label, button, check button, radio button, listbox, entry,
   textwidget, slider, menu (pulldown and popup), notebook and
   3DCanvas (for the graphics library)

Current implemented GL features are:

   zbuffer, double buffer, RGB and colorMap mode, gouraud and 
   flat shading, dithering, lighting, foging, polygon, line,
   point and string rendering, mouse and keybord input devices.
   
   The graphics library is relatively fast.

EZWGL is released under GPL. It can be found at
  ftp.x.org 
in /contrib/widgets/EZWGL.tgz


Enjoy !

