Announcing the first public release of:

                        The SpriteField Class Set
                                version 0.1
                            by Warwick Allison

The SpriteField Class Set is a collection of classes supporting multiple
simultaneous flicker-free displays of efficiently redrawn continuous and
non-continuous animated areas with the Qt GUI Toolkit (under X11). Animated
areas are two-dimensional rectangular areas upon which two-dimensional
masked raster images are in motion. Applications vary from computer games to
simulations.  

The class set is extensible to include graphic elements other than masked
raster images, such as text and geometry shapes. No such extensions are
currently provided, though there are plans to provide examples in a future
release.  

Class hierarchy:

      SpriteField 
            ImageSpriteField 
      SpriteFieldGraphic 
            VirtualSprite 
                  Sprite 
      SpriteFieldView 
      SpritePixmap 
      SpritePixmapSequence 

Got here: http://student.uq.edu.au/~s002434/qt/SpriteField/doc/html/
for this same information, and for the full source distribution.

