   The second version of Xterminal (0.003) has been released!

   Xterminal is an Object Oriented User Interface with a client-server
architecture. The main purpose is a friendly interface for the UNIX-like
operating systems. It is designed to be used to build text-based
applications, and is written in C++ using the ncurses library.
   It will consists in a complete object oriented library including
multiple, resizeable, overlapping windows, pull-down menus, dialog boxes,
buttons, scroll bars, input lines, check boxes, radio buttons, etc.
   It includes advanced object management, events handling, communications
between objects, and so on...

   Xterminal is written by:
          Dragos Acostachioaie, u950911@runner.sorosis.ro
          Adrian Teohar, cs940996@eureka.cs.tuiasi.ro,
   and is protected by the GNU General Public License.

   The maintainer of this library is Dragos Acostachioaie. Please send bug
reports, suggestions, feedback, or anything else that you think, to:
   u950911@runner.sorosis.ro (or cs930640@eureka.cs.tuiasi.ro)

   You can find the latest version of Xterminal at:
        sunsite.unc.edu, /pub/Linux/libs/Xterminal-0.003.tar.gz

   Because of the confusion with the X Toolkit (Xt) name, we renamed the 
library into Xterminal. Hope this name will fit... :-)


