What is ng2html?
================

ng2html will let you take a Norton Guide and convert it to a series of
HTML documents which you can then read using your web browser of choice.

Why bother?
===========

I use more then one OS, and it would be nice to access NGs from all of
those OSs. The common factor for all of these OSs is that they have
web browsers available. So, rather then writing my own NG reader for
each platform I decided to take the EasyWayOut(TM).

Who would want to bother?
=========================

Clipper programmers who have a Web browser (well, that's me anyway).

How much does it cost?
======================

Nothing, you are free to use it and copy it as much as you like. See
the file COPYING in the package when you download it, also, check the
header of ng2html.c for details.

What operating systems does it support?
=======================================

ng2html was developed under Linux. However, the code is written to be fairly 
generic and I have compiled it ok under Linux and Dos. With Linux I am
using GCC and with Dos I've tested it with DJGPP. If you manage to compile 
it with any other compiler or on any other OS then please let me know.

Ok, so what exactly do I need to use it?
========================================

A web browser and some Norton Guide files. You will also need a C compiler 
for your platform because I don't distribute ng2html in binary form. However, 
if you do need a binary version then let me know and I'll see what I can do 
to help.

Sounds handy, where do I download it from?
==========================================

You can download it from my web pages at:

