Stella 96 is an Atari 2600 emulator.  Currently, it is a work-in-progress 
and should be consider ALPHA level software.  However, you can play 
games starting with this release.  This release consists of a source code
distribution that's known to compile under Linux using GCC 2.7.2 (it may 
compile on other Unix machines as well).  This distribution does not 
contain any 2600 ROMs and please don't write me asking for ROMs because 
they're copyrighted!  If you own any of the Activision Action Packs you
can use the ROM images from it with Stella 96.

Supported Systems
=================

Stella 96 is currently supported on the following systems:

  * Linux 1.x.x (SVGALIB, X-Windows)

  * Stella 96 should compile under most Unix operating systems as long as
    it has X-Windows install.  However, the current support for using the
    keyboard as a joystick is not very good.

Required Software/Hardware
==========================

Stella 96 requires the following software and hardware:

  * ANSI C++ Compiler (GCC 2.7.2 is known to work)

  * SVGALIB and/or X-Windows

  * Linux kernel joystick driver (not really required but strongly suggested)

  * 2600 ROM images

  * At least a 486 DX4 100 with a fast video card

Distribution Site
================= 

The Stella 96 distribution can be obtained from the Stella 96 home page at:

  http://www4.ncsu.edu/~bwmott/www/2600

Contacts
========

If you have any questions regarding Stella 96 send mail to:

  bwmott@eos.ncsu.edu



