ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/X11/xutils/dxpc-0.9.tar.gz.

dxpc (Differential X Protocol Compressor) is an X11 protocol
compressor that speeds up X over slow network links (like
dialup PPP connections).


from the README file:

   1. WHAT'S NEW IN THIS RELEASE
      ==========================

   * Miscellaneous compression improvements (dxpc version 0.9 achieves
     about 3:1 compression on many X programs that I use.  The compression
     ratios for different applications may vary widely, however.)

   * Makefiles for more UNIXes

   * Miscellaneous dxpc_client improvements:
     * Now creates /tmp/.X11-unix directory if it doesn't  already exist
     * Fix for server host specified by IP addr on systems where gethostbyname
       doesn't accept IP addresses
     * dxpc_client now verifies that server IP addr or hostname is valid
       at startup, rather than waiting until an X client starts up

   * Miscellaneous dxpc_server improvements:
     * On HP-UX, dxpc_server now looks for the real X server's UNIX domain
       socket in /usr/spool/sockets if it isn't found in /tmp/.X11-unix.

   * Finally, some tips on using xauth-based authorization with dxpc



