Ovidius GmbH announces the release of MetaMorphosis-free Version 2.1

MetaMorphosis is an SGML tree transformer. Some of its features
are:

* MM works always in tree mode; this allows unlimited context
  access during transformation

* MM is target-driven; i.e. a MM program specifies directly
  the structure of the target tree

* MM has a declarative query and transformation language

MetaMorphosis-free is a functionally unrestricted version of
MetaMorphosis. It is available only for the Linux operating
system. MetaMorphosis-free is governed by a special license.

MetaMorphosis-free has three built-in backends:

* SGML, allows to convert the internal tree to SGML; supports
  start and end tag omission

* TEXT, reads out the tree and can be used to pre- and suffix the 
  elements with arbitrary text

* DUMP, generates a very verbose external representation of the
  internal tree in the EMACS outline format. This can be used
  for structure control and debugging

This is a selection of some of the new features in Version 2.1:

* handling of SDATA entities and PIs as nodes

* support of indices; an index can hold anything which can
  be the result of a MM query (strings, attributes, nodes, ...)
  indices can be used to access large sets of data very
  fast

* built-in pacing mode allows to interactively step through
  transformations, move around in the tree, etc.

* the script compiler and many functions have been optimized; they
  perform now twice as fast as before



For more information see

http://www.ovidius.com/mm-free.html

>From there you can download MM-free, a PostScript Version of the
manual and the tutorial, and the data files for the tutorial.

There is an online manual (http://www.ovidius.com/mmmanual/toc.html, 
the manual is still for Version 2.0 but will be upgraded in the
next few days) and an online tutorial (http://www.ovidius.com/mmtut/toc.html)

Questions? Problems? Send mail to info@ovidius.com
