DISLIN for Linux - gcc 2.7.0, g77 and f2c

DISLIN is a high level and easy to use graphics library for displaying
data as curves, bar graphs, pie charts, 3D-colour plots, surfaces,
contours and maps. The software is available for several C and Fortran
compilers and hardware platforms.

A free version for Linux (compiled with gcc 2.7.0) can be found in

     ftp://linhmi.mpae.gwdg.de/pub/dislin/dislin_linux_1.62.tar.gz
     ftp://linhmi.mpae.gwdg.de/pub/dislin/dislin_linux_2.62.tar.gz

The distribution contains interface routines for programming in Fortran
with f2c or g77.

