You can download Laserjet Manger from sunsite (currently in Incomming,
but will probably move to the following location):

    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/system/Printing/ljetmgr2.1.lsm
    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/system/Printing/ljetmgr2.1.tar.gz


3. INSTALLATION

This is a ready to run application - unpack the tar archive, maybe add
the 'bin' directory to your path and start the program 

        ??/SW/bin/ljetmgr

users in german speaking countries should set LANG or SOFTLANG to
'german' ;-)

4. DOCUMENTATION
Complete documentation and context sensitive help is included in
HTML-format. A postscript version is available too.


5. COPYRIGHT
This software falls under the GNU public license. See the
documentation for further details.


