What is 'ears'?
***************
A GPL'd program that can recognize spoken words.  You write a list of 
words or use a default one.  You speak those words into your sound card 
mic each three times (train_ears).  You speak the same words and the 
program (listen) shows what you have said.  If you have the guts, drive 
your shell with it.

What is new in version 0.22?
****************************
This is mainly a bugfix release after the fresh 0.20.  I didn't expect
as much differences between Linux-aout and Linux-elf.  
o  it should now compile on all systems having the libs mentioned below
o  libg++.a is no longer needed
o  elf binaries are available, finally

What platforms are supported?
*****************************
The source supports systems with the Voxware sound driver and systems 
that have AF sound tools.  To compile, you need gcc-2.7.0 or 2.7.2 and 
up, libstdc++.a from libg++-2.7.0.x and up, libncurses.a/libpanel.a from 
ncurses-1.9.8a and up.

Where can I get it?
*******************
    ftp://svr-ftp.eng.cam.ac.uk/pub/comp.speech/recognition
    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu_and_mirrors/.../apps/sound/speech

