Dmsdos filesystem for Linux:

Dmsdosfs is a filesystem extension for Linux. It allows mounting compressed
dos/win95 partitions under Linux.

Dmsdosfs "converts" the large, hidden files DBLSPACE.* or DRVSPACE.* into
subdirectories wherein you can find the whole compressed filesystem.

   - supports:
         * dos 6.x doublespace
         * dos 6.22 drivespace
         * win95 doublespace
         * win95 drivespace 3 (this one with some restrictions)

   - new in this release:
         * long filename support even in uncompressed host partition
           (requires a recent 1.3.xx kernel)
         * new mmap code to support the writable mmap feature of recent
           kernels (requires a recent 1.3.xx kernel)
         * some bugs fixed

   - still missing:
         * module support (under construction, should be in next release)
         * write access speedup (planned)

Note: This is the last dmsdosfs release that supports Linux kernel 1.2.13
      and older 1.3.xx (xx<81) kernels.

If you can't find it on the ftp servers listed below, try the incoming
directories.

Frank

