This package is the original sh-utils-1.12 package with a few
changes to su to support wheel groups. (Allowing  you to limit
who may su to root) and a double check on the password so that
users may not log in with an old password if they ran su before
the password was changed, as was possible in the previous su.

It also contains a c program version of false. Some system administrators
will set a users login shell to /bin/false. This was a potential security
hole when /bin/sh was actually a link to bash.

	Eric Kuzniar

