Wrox Press are looking for additional technical reviewers for their new
book, due out in the summer. : 

Beginning Linux Programming

>From the authors of Instant Unix (ISBN 1-874416-65-6), this book uses C 
to show how to get the most from your Linux system. As such it is aimed 
at Webmasters and system administrators who need to develop small, custom
applications, and anyone who wants to really get to grips with UNIX. 

Adopting a practical 'Try-It-Out' tutorial style, the book explains 
the Linux environment (using a version of Linux FT provided on the book's 
CD), and then progresses to fundamental UNIX concepts - shells, files, 
terminals, processes, signals, pipes, messages, sockets, and thence to 
graphics (using Tcl/Tk) and a practical implementation of a CGI application.

The technical reviewers need to understand all these concepts, in order to
objectively (and sometimes subjectively!) criticise the manuscript for its
technical content and accuracy, the subject coverage and structure.

Interested? Then mail me (timb@wrox.com) for more details.


Timothy Briggs

Technical Editor, Wrox Press.


