The Pver commercial Verilog hardware description language (HDL) digital
electronic simulator is available on Linux.   It implements the
entire IEEE P1364 standard Verilog language.  Although the entry price
of $995 is high for Linux software, it is a fraction of the cost of
Verilog simulators on workstations.   Also see ftp site ftp.crl.com
in directory /ftp/users/pv/pverhelp for more information.  Here is the
data sheet:

- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pver - Verilog Simulator

					     Pragmatic C Software

- -----------------------------------------------------------------

Description

   o Implements Full IEEE P1364 Standard Verilog Language
     Pver is a full IEEE P1364 Verilog HDL Standard  simula-
     tor.   PLI 2.0 and PLI 1.0 tf_ routine programming lan-
     guage interface included.

   o Text Based Simulator with	Added  Programming  Language
     Style Debugger
     Pver  includes  an	 integrated text based debugger that
     follows GDB style syntax modified for  design  instance
     trees  providing  users who are already proficient with
     programming language debuggers such as  GDB  or  DBX  a
     familiar  debugging  environment.	 Pver  is  aimed  at
     designers who prefer the Unix workstation	"combination
     of	 multiple  specialized	tools" design approach.	 All
     input can be entered  interactively  or  supplied	from
     scripts.	 Pver  is  not recommended for designers who
     prefer a mouse and menu  based  integrated	 development
     environment.   Pver  does not yet contain an integrated
     wave form viewer.	However, third party wave  form	 and
     menu tools can be used with Pver through the VCD (value
     change dump file) and by linking with third  party	 PLI
     based tools.

   o Fast Development Cycle and Easy to Use PLI
     Pver  is  a stand alone interpretive Verilog simulator.
     Translation requires only one pass.   Therefore,  no  C
     compilation  or linking with other programs is required
     before simulation can begin.  A C (or C++) compiler and
     unix  style  utilities are required to use the PLI, but
     linking user PLI C language models requires adding only
     the  pverobj.o  included  object version of Pver to the
     link command.  Debugging user C models is	as  easy  as
     debugging	stand alone C programs that use a predefined
     API (application program  interface)  from	 a  library.
     Because  Pver  is an interpreter, there is no long wait
     for a large C compilation to complete  before  starting
     simulation.

   o Fast Simulation with Small Memory Usage
     Unlike  some  other simulators, Pver does not slow down
     if large designs are simulated because only one copy of
     each module is stored and because nets and memories are
     packed to the bit.	 Inout ports are  implemented  using
     transistor switch channel algorithm.  Pver on work sta-
     tions is usable on the largest designs.  Pver's simula-
     tion event processing rate is comparable to the fastest
     P1364 compliant Verilog simulators (requires  Pver	 Pro
     version  accelerator).   Pver offers a gate eater opti-
     mization that can reduce simulation time on  unfinished
     designs.

   o Low Pricing with Superior Price Performance Ratio
     Pver pricing is below that of competing Verilog simula-
     tors  and approaches computer programming language com-
     piler pricing.  Pver price performance is	at  least  3
     times  that  of  any  other complete IEEE P1364 Verilog
     simulator.	 Pver Entry product offers a full P1364 com-
     pliant simulator without any design size limitation for
     under $1000.  Pver entry can be upgraded  to  add	more
     features  when  more  capabilities	 are  needed.	Pver
     includes lint style checking  much	 of  which  requires
     building	the  optimized	simulation  data  structure.
     Therefore, Pver offers simulation and lint style check-
     ing  at  a	 price lower than many non simulating syntax
     checkers.


Three Different Pver Products Available

   o Entry Level Simulator for under $1000
     Pver Entry product offers full IEEE P1364 Verilog simu-
     lator  personal  (assigned	 to  one  user) licenses for
     $995.  Strengths and full timing features are included,
     and  there	 are no design size limitations.  Pver Entry
     does not include either PLI 1.0 or	 2.0  or  SDF  delay
     back  annotation.	 An  integrated wave viewer is under
     development.  Pver contains  some	added  system  tasks
     (not  part	 of  P1364 standard) which approximate delay
     setting and PLI 1.0 like functionality of	more  expen-
     sive versions of Pver.

     Before  purchasing a competing low priced Verilog simu-
     lator, you may want to determine if the following	fea-
     tures  are supported:  Are strengths simulated for mod-
     els that use tri-state busses and	pullups?   Do  bufif
     gates  support  L	and  H	values?	 Is glitch detection
     implemented to catch circuit timing problems?  Does the
     simulator	impose	arbitrary  design  size	 limits?  Is
     interactive entry of Verilog  statements  supported  to
     allow interactive debugging?

   o FPGA Simulator for under $2400
     Pver Standard product adds support for PLI 1.0 tf_ rou-
     tines (allows PLI C coded tasks and functions) and sup-
     port  for	SDF  (standard	delay format 3.1) delay file
     back annotation that is still under development.	Sup-
     port for standard -v and -y part libraries is included.
     Price for personal Pver Standard (assigned to one user)
     licenses  is  $2395.  Pver Standard product is intended
     to provide all features needed for FPGA simulation.

   o Pver Pro Leading Edge Simulator for under $3600
     Pver Pro product adds new PLI 2.0 vpi_  routine  inter-
     face  and	a  gate	 level optimizer that can accelerate
     simulation of simply connected gates by as much as	 two
     times.  Development of a behavioral statement optimizer
     is in progress.  Only Pver Pro and Verilog XL currently
     implement	PLI 2.0 vpi_ routines.	Pver Pro includes an
     examples directory with thousands of lines	 of  C	code
     illustrating  PLI	2.0  features.	 Price	for personal
     (assigned to one user) Pver Pro licenses is $3595.

   o Supported Hardware Platforms
     Available on Linux (a.out).

